# Gitleaks findings in git history that have been reviewed. Used by the
# `secrets` job in .github/workflows/security.yml.
#
# Each line is a finding's fingerprint: <commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>.
# A fingerprint never contains the secret itself. Old commits can't be changed
# (the repo is public, so rewriting history wouldn't un-leak anything), so a
# real secret is fixed by revoking/rotating it, then listed here with a note.
#
# Never add a fingerprint without a comment saying why it's safe.

